// Full gas momentum closure (distributed pressure momentum): a rate-driven
// vertical riser with the ideal-gas EOS on and closure model "full". The
// per-section slip state is driven by the gas momentum balance with the
// local mixture-row pressure gradient substituted (the gas share alpha_g dp
// with the proportional wall split alpha_g fr cancelling it), and the gas
// material acceleration dvG/dt = aM + alpha ds/dt + vG dvG/dx expanded,
// which reduces to
//   ds/dt = [(rho_m - rhoG)(g sinT + aM) - rhoG vG dvG/dx
//            - sigma/alpha_g]/(alpha rhoG),
// sigma = C s|s| semi-implicit through the origin secant. The convective
// term (forward difference, zero gradient at the outlet face) is active
// through the front-propagation transient and vanishes identically at the
// uniform fixed point, so the terminal slip is s* = sign(R) sqrt(alpha_g
// |R| / C) with R = (rho_m - rhoG) g sinT (du/dt = 0 for a rate-driven
// line). Wall friction rides the pressure field: the drive carries
// buoyancy, mixture acceleration and gas convection only.
//
// Closed-form steady state (volume conservation pins the phase fluxes at
// the injected rates, and the gas mass flux in = out at the injected
// reference density pins rhoG* = rhoG = 500 exactly, hence the EOS pressure
// p* = rhoG gasR T0 = 1.5e8 Pa uniform):
//   rho_m - rhoG = alpha (rhoL - rhoG) = 500 alpha
//   s* = sqrt(alpha_g alpha (rhoL - rhoG) g / C)   (C = 1000, sinT = 1)
//   F(alpha*, s*) = vsl = 0.15   (liquid volume flux pins the holdup)
// The (alpha*, s*) pair is a coupled fixed point solved by iteration here:
// alpha* = 0.776065, s* = 0.923114 (checker root-finds independently).
// The heavy artificial gas (rhoG 500, gasR 1000) makes the slip ODE
// genuinely inertial at dt 0.05 (rate dt ~ 1), exercising the implicit
// Euler relaxation instead of a quasi-algebraic terminal pin. The
// buoyancy-driven fallback keeps the bulk liquid flux negative through
// much of the transient (liquid actually flows down while the gas rushes
// past), so the injected-cut front needs ~350 s to fully flush - hence
// the long endTime.
//
// tests/check_two_fluid.py mode fullmomentum replicates the coupled slip +
// Godunov holdup + water + gas mass recursion cell by cell (1e-9), checks
// vsl + vsg = vm and p = rhoG gasR T0 per section, the Churchill + gravity
// drop, the pnode march from the outlet anchor, and the uniform steady
// state (alpha*, s*, rhoG* = 500, flushed water cut).
//
// Measured anchors (dt 0.05, endTime 400): steady alpha* = 0.776065,
// s* = 0.923114, EOS pressure 1.500000e8 Pa, water cut flushed to 0.3.
fluid
{
    rhoL 1000;
    rhoG 500;
    muL  0.01;
    muG  1e-5;
    gasR 1000;
}

pipe
{
    length 20;
    diameter 0.02;
    roughness 0;
    angleDeg 90;
    sections 20;
}

closure
{
    model full;
    interfacialDrag 1000;
}

initial
{
    alpha 0.5;
    water 0.8;
    temperature 300;
}

boundaries
{
    inlet  { type phaseRates; vsl 0.15; vsg 0.25; waterFraction 0.3; }
    outlet { type fixedPressure; p 1.5e8; }  // absolute with the EOS on;
                                             // only the backflow ghost uses
                                             // it (G >= 0 throughout)
}

time
{
    dt 0.05;
    endTime 400;
    reportEvery 400;
}
